course: dictionary
lesson: 2649
title: Words that stop things happening
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A deterrent is something that makes people decide not to do a thing, because the trouble or danger it would bring is too big. The word comes from deter, which means to put someone off. Look for it in the context: «The deterrent» is the British official way to say nuclear weapons, the most destructive bombs ever made. The sentence tells you why they exist: so that other countries are afraid to attack.
explain: Deterrent can be a noun (a deterrent) or an adjective that describes an effect (a deterrent effect). The phrases around it give clues too: «act as a deterrent», «a strong deterrent», «a deterrent to crime». In each one, something is in place to stop a bad thing before it happens.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If you read «a strong reason to stop» instead of «a strong deterrent» and it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
fact: Deterrent (noun) means something that makes people decide not to do a thing.
fact: As an adjective, deterrent describes the effect: a deterrent effect stops people before they act.
fact: «A deterrent to crime» means something that stops crime before it happens.
fact: An animal's bad taste is a deterrent to predators, so the predators decide not to eat it.
exercise: «The thick fence is a strong deterrent to climbers.» What does a strong deterrent mean here? | *Something that stops climbers from trying | A loud sound made by the fence | Something that helps climbers reach the top | A kind of climbing rope
exercise: «An animal's bad taste is a deterrent to predators.» What does the bad taste do to predators? | Makes them hungrier | *Makes them decide not to attack | Makes them fall asleep | Makes them come closer
exercise: «A deterrent effect» uses deterrent to describe the effect. What word class is deterrent in this phrase? | A noun | *An adjective | A verb | An adverb
test: What does «a deterrent to crime» mean? | A type of crime | A place where crime is solved | *Something that stops crime before it happens | A very loud alarm that rings after a crime
test: Which country might keep weapons as a deterrent, according to the meaning? | A country that wants to sell its food | A country that wants a holiday by the sea | A country that wants to make its roads bigger | *A country that wants others to be afraid to attack it
exam: Why is something a deterrent, according to the meaning? | Because it has no effect on anyone at all | Because it is very old and valuable | Because it makes people laugh and feel happy | *Because it makes people decide not to do a thing, due to the trouble or danger it would bring
